  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on identifying which lottery has a sure outcome and preferring that one. The relevant information — the 100% probability of 2400€ in Lottery B — is present in the problem and could have been considered. However, the individual does not refer to the certainty of Lottery B at all. Instead, the deliberation centers on the higher payoff in A and the smallness of the risk of getting nothing. The individual seems to accept risk for a higher gain, which is contrary to the logic of preferring sure outcomes. There is no indication that the presence or absence of a sure outcome played any role in the decision. Therefore, the information relevant to the decision reason (sureness) was not considered, and the justification (chasing higher gain with minimal risk) does not align with the reason’s rule (prefer sure outcome).",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
}

